Bugfix: The log viewer keeps its list consistent after errors and fits narrow screens

When reloading the log viewer after a filter change failed - for example
because the 60 requests per minute were used up - the entries of the previous
filter stayed in the list together with "Load more", which then appended
entries of the new filter from the old position. A failed reload now empties
the list and hides "Load more". A failed "Load more" keeps the entries and can
be retried with the same filter. Answers to requests that a newer filter
replaced are still discarded.

The error message now names the cause: the waiting time from Retry-After when
there were too many requests, missing admin rights, or a log file that is not
available. Screen readers announce it right away, separately from the status
line.

On narrow screens - phones, but also tablets next to the navigation - the table
no longer pushes the page sideways. When the list is narrower than the table
needs, each entry is shown as a card: time, level and app, the message below,
user and request at the end. Opened details, including stack traces, fit the
screen. Both log level selections shrink with the screen, and long app names
and user IDs wrap.

Stack trace boxes can be reached with the keyboard and are named ("Trace",
"Trace (cause 1)", ...). Paths, traces and other log data keep their
left-to-right order on right-to-left pages.
